      "source": [
        {
          "question": "e-459",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "If we let $u=1-3x,$ then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} = -3\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d x = -\\dfrac 1 3 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nThen, we can write the integral in terms of $u$ and evaluate:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {e}^{1-3x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{u}\\cdot (-\\frac{1}{3})\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{u}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{1-3x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14007647/example-459.json",
          "file_sha256": "2d4876ba083fff19532693ea4c70afb24dfe9d6c82ce7a7f60711a984783bebf"
